node.doctext:
I'm unclear on the concept of 'our'. I have a module, <code>package foo;</code>, that several different programs <code>use</code>. I want <b>foo</b> to contain the definition of a constant scalar <b>bar</b> that programs using <b>foo</b> can reference.
<p>
<b>foo.pm</b>
<code>
package foo;
our $bar = 42;
1;
</code>
<b>pgm.pl</b>
<code>
#!/usr/bin/env perl
use 5.36;
use foo;
# 'our $bar'? 'our $foo::bar'? 'my $foo::bar'?
say $bar;
</code>
I've tried several variations on declaring $bar in <b>pgm.pl</b> (including not declaring it at all) without successfully referencing the value that was set in <b>package foo</b>.
<p>
Could some kind monk straighten me out? Is this even what 'our' is meant for?
